{
	chapter.1BA63B3D442634F3.title: "Foregone Industry"
	chapter.42E5151EE62182CC.title: "... Everything In Its Place"
	chapter.434B390999A6EA0E.title: "Synthesizing Resources"
	chapter.43D354AD3B952ABF.title: "Dire Times, 20 Wolves"
	chapter.4B1229F34CDBAF10.title: "A Place For Everything..."
	chapter.4FD7E205ED15677C.title: "Laying the Foundations"
	chapter.5E041E7746FAF97D.title: "Mob Boxes, An Offer You Can't Refuse"
	chapter.6205698F2556C84F.title: "Dynamically Integrated"
	chapter.68264299A2F01768.title: "There was a goal afterall"
	chapter.6DD5238D54AAB5B3.title: "End of the IO As We Know It"
	chapter.7FA6E94DC1AFAD57.title: "Fluxuating Empowahment"
	quest.00FC75F7F3FD5DE0.quest_desc: [
		"We're on the way! I'll see you in a minute!"
		""
		"Thank you for all your help!"
	]
	quest.01BC305C929B90AF.quest_desc: [
		"This is an upgrade base for your &bBackpack&r."
		""
		"With a little work you'll find that &bBackpack&r and storage upgrades are interchangeable."
	]
	quest.030C5514F23CF444.quest_desc: [
		"Okay, now take that &bGranite&r you've been making and the &bHoney Bottle&r you collected and right-click one with the other."
		""
		"Didn't work? Try right-clicking the other one with the other one."
		""
		"Boom - &bCopper Ore&r! Break that and get yourself some &bRaw Copper&r!"
	]
	quest.03422F73507E8C92.quest_desc: [
		"Storage is going to be important, because you are going to pick up so much stuff!"
		""
		"So why not make it easier on yourself, by whipping up a &bStorage Bank&r! Yes, I said bank. This little baby can hold up to 9 different things and four stacks of those 9 things. Get to crafting!"
		""
		"For the liquidly minded of you, there's also a fluid version of the bank called &bThe Tank&r. You can make one if you want to, especially if you want to finish this quest!"
	]
	quest.03DB23461BB43688.quest_desc: [
		"Higher tier machines need higher tier &bMachine Frames&r. If you're making this, you should have some of your stuff automated by now, which is good, because making these guys is a bit of a process. "
		""
		"But, if you want to get to &bVoidshimmer Goo&r (we'll get to that soon) you're going to need one of these. "
	]
	quest.042E7A8E38C63058.quest_desc: ["These guys here, after linking with your storage controller, will allow you to pipe or hopper directly to and from your storage system."]
	quest.0476B88E0F9C0491.quest_desc: [
		"Got some &bCharcoal&r? Good. Probably a good idea to keep that going if you can because without &bCoal&r, you're going to need it."
		""
		"Let's test to make sure that &bFurnace&r of yours is working properly. Throw some &bCobblestone&r in it and turn it back to &bStone&r. I'd suggest making a lot of this now. You're going to need it later."
	]
	quest.054D49D72F346E1F.quest_desc: [
		"The &bDisk Drive&r houses all the &bDisks&r that you are bound to be making to keep your AE2 system really chugging along. "
		""
		"Make one of these and you're good to go!"
	]
	quest.05A6989623B53C03.quest_desc: [
		"If you want to make this thing work faster, or enhance the items you get from specific monsters, make one (or up to four) of these upgrades and add them to your mob farm. They'll work to get you better materials and some of them are tailored to specific mobs. "
		""
		"The rest is up to you!"
	]
	quest.05E8B94B9E6E5AB6.quest_desc: [
		"Need to move items? Make yourself some of these!"
		""
		"There are upgrades for this so that you can filter out items, extract faster etc."
		""
		"Plus, like all the Ender IO conduits, you can place multiples of these into the same block space! "
	]
	quest.0602AF31A0AD48FB.quest_desc: [
		"Attach the &bStorage Terminal&r to any of your &bLogic Cables&r and if everything went well, you should have access to your entire system. If not, you did something wrong. Or I described it badly. "
		""
		"Either way, check everything is connected properly, click on the Crafting Table tab on the top left and biggity bam, whose the human? You are! Unless you're not human, in which case I COME IN PEACE."
	]
	quest.06609BBE91DC666F.quest_desc: ["The Pattern Encoding Terminal is used to make recipes for auto crafting. If you want to really get into automation, you're going to need this machine."]
	quest.07BD5E553FBC124A.quest_desc: [
		"Okay, this thing is important so make sure you listen very carefully. "
		""
		"Previously, I got you to make some &bSmooth Stone&r. I hope you made a lot of it! You'll need some &bGlass&r, too, so grab some of that and make a &bStone Block Generator&r. Heck, make a few of 'em. They're going to come in handy!"
		""
		"We can program this thing to automatically spit out almost any type of stone that you can think of, straight into any container you put on top of it. We're going to need a lot of different types of stone for what I have in mind!"
		""
		"Also, have a look around the village. You should find remnants of what &6Newstone Hollow&r used to be. Maybe there's some old &bIron&r tools somewhere you can throw into that salvager of yours to make a bucket. Maybe there's even a bucket so you don't need to salvage anything at all!"
	]
	quest.08133F18BA06E605.quest_desc: [
		"Burn &bbedrock&r burn, Ender I(nfern)O!"
		""
		"Hit some &bBedrock&r with fire, wait until you hear it pop and grab yourself some &bGrains of Infinity&r! The cornerstone of any nutritious breakfast."
		""
		"I mean, of Ender IO machinery. Yeah, that's what I meant to say."
	]
	quest.08322DB2E353F4B3.quest_desc: ["Did you know that Sophisticated Storage does portable storage too? Well it does! Get some leather and other stuff and make yourself a fully upgradable &bBackpack&r that you'll wonder how you ever did without. I promise!"]
	quest.0A551CB99A98E744.quest_desc: [
		"Use your &bVoid Chassis&r to make an &bAlloy Smelter&r. Any of them will do."
		""
		"Add a good &bCapacitor&r to this thing and it'll cook stuff faster than you can see it. No more waiting around for those slow, old, vanilla &bFurnace&rs to cook things up. You can also use it to make alloys, mixing certain materials into other materials. This will open up a whole new world of possibilities!"
		""
		"Don't forget, Ender IO has a lot of useful machines that you can use to assist you on your journey. You don't have to stop at just this one!"
	]
	quest.0E215DA535D4D9C1.quest_desc: [
		"Now here's where the magic begins!"
		""
		"Your &bStone Block Generator&r should be producing stone by now. If not, flip back to the last quest or check in JEI to make sure you have everything set up correctly. "
		""
		"Place one of your new &bStone Blocks&r on the ground and hold some &bFlint&r in your hand. Now, right click the &bStone&r with the &bFlint&r and if my calculations are correct, it should turn in to &bCoal Ore&r! Break it and get the &bCoal&r which you have worked so hard to make!"
	]
	quest.103199D75DBDC7A5.quest_desc: [
		"Back to that mythical \"Nether\" place. I've seen no evidence to confirm it exists, but you will find a lot of &bBasalt&r in there!"
		""
		"Get a bunch of it and some of that &bGold&r you've been making."
	]
	quest.10C98E73946CC03C.quest_desc: [
		"Want to send power to yourself wirelessly? If only there were such a thing! However, make one of these and your wireless network awaits. This is the heart and soul of the whole operation. Use it with care! "
		""
		"Config it properly and make sure it remains powered and you can have as much wireless power as you need!"
	]
	quest.11B985E986E67894.quest_desc: [
		"Digital storage! It's all the rage with the kids. Think of it as cloud storage without using other people's computers! It's as simple as that!"
		""
		"Make yourself an &bME Controller&r to get your digital storage underway. Legends tell of a more refined storage system, which has sadly been lost to the ages. "
	]
	quest.1479E9BED62FB3E1.quest_desc: [
		"&bShadowpulse Goo&r could be a little harder to get because you're going to have to find a big angry dude called The Warden. You'll find him in the Deep Dark biome. Haven't found one yet? Check out the Nature's Compass for directions!"
		""
		"Now, you &ocould&r avoid fighting this guy if you're really, really quiet. What you're looking for down there is &bEcho Shards&r, &bSculk Shriekers&r and &bSculk&r. You can mine most of that with silk touch on a &bHoe&r."
		""
		"By the way, you can get enchantments off gear by dropping the item and a &bBook&r (or a couple of books) onto an &bObsidian Block&r and then dropping an &bAnvil&r on top. Easy way to get that silk touch enchant! "
	]
	quest.15989664A4077372.quest_desc: ["Storage components become part of disks. Bigger disks hold more stuffs. The toppest drive is effectively infinite storage! But you'll have to work for it. You're gonna need so many of these things, you may as well start making them now."]
	quest.163AAB1DF68BFE25.quest_desc: ["That &bRed Dye&r and &bRed Sandstone&r will make &bRedstone Ore&r, the reddest of all the stones! Make it, break it, collect your reward!"]
	quest.199215FE1642F634.quest_desc: [
		"It's time for us to talk seriously about where we're going with all of this stuff you're making for me. "
		""
		"If we can get the right resources together, we're going to use them to make a machine that will hopefully bring us back! You'll need at least one of these &bSupreme Machine Frames&r in order to do that, because we'll need this to make &bShadowpulse Goo&r (we'll get to that)."
	]
	quest.1A8F81227016ADA9.quest_desc: [
		"&bEnergy Cables&r, stick with me here, carry energy around. If you want to send Powah from one location to another and haven't figure out how to do it wirelessly, this is what you'll need."
		""
		"This tier will move 2,000 RF per tick and the top tier will transport 1,000,000 RF per tick! Crazy town!"
	]
	quest.1A962341CEC446A3.quest_desc: ["Made yourself a &bMob Farm&r? Time to set it up for the mob you want to generate resources from. Each type of mob has their own biome, so if you were making a cow farm for example, you would need to make an &bAnimal Plains Farm&r. If you were making one for Blazes, you'd need a &bNether Fortress Farm&r. You get the idea, now get to crafting! Any of these will do."]
	quest.1B2F342369133229.quest_desc: [
		"Our machine is going to need a lot of power, so we'll make a couple of these batteries that have unlimited power in them! Muahahahaha! "
		""
		"Anyway, make two and we'll pretend that I didn't say that. Look over there!"
	]
	quest.1BCD4C3F66AAB0F1.quest_desc: ["Now with exciting block conversion action! 83.662% more exciting than paint drying!"]
	quest.1BE114B2C9F2E02F.quest_desc: [
		"When I was a kid, I used to read a lot of science fiction. That gave me a wicked idea! What if you could send Powah wirelessly directly to a person so that they could keep any devices they had on them fully charged. Cell phones, &bBlock Exchangers&r, &bWirless Terminals&r and stuff. You know? The usual stuff. Make one of these and you never have to worry about manually charging anything again. "
		""
		"Unless, of course, you run out of powah. "
	]
	quest.1CAB038ED8EA610D.quest_desc: [
		"That worked?! Excellent! We're well on the way!"
		""
		"Grab some of that &bStone&r and run it through the &bFurnace&r one more time. It'll make another type of &bStone&r, &bSmooth Stone&r, and we'll be able to use that to really push things along!"
	]
	quest.1E432C3C539EC925.quest_desc: [
		"The &bSimple Machine Frame&r is a better version of the &bPity Machine Frame&r. Make one of them if you want to make more advanced machines. Make several why not?"
		""
		"You're also going to need one of these if you want to get in to &bBlazegloom Goo&r, but we'll come back to that in a bit. Get cracking!"
	]
	quest.1EA1A74253B238F5.quest_desc: ["The ever-so-slightly radioactive &bFermented &bSpider Eye&r on a &bCalcite&r block makes &bUraninite&r!"]
	quest.205DA6AFAC557E2A.quest_desc: [
		"The toppest of all the tiers of Dire items, the &bEclipse Alloy&r. "
		""
		"The gear you can make with this stuff is properly top tier, and if you add the right upgrades you can make yoursellf invincible to damage, fire, falling and even have the ability to fly! "
	]
	quest.209226F8CFD2FF7C.quest_desc: ["While you're in this \"Nether\" I keep hearing about, you might as well grab a bunch of &bNetherrack&r as well. I hear there's also a lot of &bBone Blocks&r there, too. Grab some of that as well!"]
	quest.21ACA8FD46271508.quest_desc: [
		"Not to disillusion you, but in order for you to get to the higher tiers of machine frames, you're going to need to make a &bDissolution Chamber&r. To do this, you first will need to make some &bPlastic&r, which you can make from the &bLatex&r that you just picked up. It just makes sense!"
		""
		"I promise!"
	]
	quest.2285F83709105747.quest_desc: ["Remember that &bItem Interface&r that you made a couple of minutes ago? Well, now you need to connect it to something. And that something is some cables! &bLogic Cables&r to be precise. Make a bunch of these, you'll probably need them."]
	quest.232935DF902AC0AA.quest_desc: [
		"You're definitely going to want to upgrade your gear at some point, and what better way than by using &bIron&r?"
		""
		"So what's a rich source of &bIron&r, I hear you ask? I'll tell you. It's &bRed Meat&r! Yes, the humble &bCow&r once again comes to the rescue. Thank you, humble &bCow&r."
		""
		"You're also going to need some &bTuff&r, which you can find right there in the ground under your feet!"
	]
	quest.241F24892D422EC9.quest_desc: ["&bDiamonds&r! Yes, energize yourself some &bDiamonds&r to make &bNiotic Crystals&r. These will get you to an even higher tier of Powah production. Higher tiers = more Powah!"]
	quest.254D1BEB5F60C273.quest_desc: ["Okay, now stick with me here. Remember how the last two drawers did 2048 items? Well, this one does too! But this time you can store up to 4 different items, 512 of each."]
	quest.25FC9DFDDE9D9A8C.quest_desc: [
		"Time to find some &bRed Dye&r. Luckily there's a few ways to get it - &bPoppies&r, &bBeets&r, &bRose Bushes&r. I'd say for this one, you're probably going to want to get some sort of farm going. "
		""
		"You're also going to need a lot of &bRed Sandstone&r. &bRed Sandstone&r can be found in your nearest &bBadlands Biome&r, or by crushing &bTerracotta&r in your &bSqueezer&r or &bMill&r of choice. If you're lucky, you can even find some &bRed Sandstone&r out in your world hiding under the &bRed Sand&r!"
		""
		"Once you have enough, come and meet me back here. I'll be waiting!"
	]
	quest.2BBE4F9E4A61B988.quest_desc: [
		"You know how when you're running around and you see like these tall, light blue trees? Well they are totally useful! In fact, you can do all sorts of wonderful things with them. Like make a storage system! Like we're going to do right now! Live! And in color!"
		""
		"Before you can get too far, you will need to make some stuff. This stuff is important, so make sure you pay attention. Yes, you!"
	]
	quest.2C6EB5919C65157A.quest_desc: [
		"You might want to build up to this one a little, because you're going to have to do some boss fighting. "
		""
		"&bNether Star&r, &bBlazing Blocks&r and &bRedstone Blocks&r are all required. Plus, a LOT of RFs! "
		""
		"Oh, but the returns you will see! It's all worth it, I promise!"
	]
	quest.2CF98E41BF91E172.quest_desc: ["What good is an AE2 system if you can't see anything inside it?"]
	quest.2D0190B5AFB7EF1F.quest_desc: ["Want to make sure that your drawers never get backed up? Make one of these! Once your drawer hits its max limit, this card will make sure that any extras get discarded. Great for when you have more of something than you'll ever be able to use. "]
	quest.2EE1D64AFC7ACCE5.quest_desc: [
		"What we have in mind here means that we need to transport things across dimensions. Thusly, we need a &bDimensional Chest&r. But you'll also need a &bDimensional Tank&r. That's for transporting fluids across dimensions, and we all know the human body is, like, 70% fluids! "
		""
		"Don't think too much about the implications of that, just make a &bDimensional Tank&r and &bDimensional Chest&r!"
	]
	quest.306BBC2715EEF07A.quest_desc: [
		"&bVoidshimmer Goo&r takes a little bit of work. You're going to have to go to The End, fight the massive dragon there and during that fight, collect some of its &bBreath&r and use that to make the next tier of goo. "
		""
		"Keep going! Only one more to goo!"
	]
	quest.3074E32F11066B3A.quest_desc: [
		"This little guy right here is going to come in invaluable. The &bSophisticated Storage Controller&r. You can hook up as many &bSophisticated Chests&r, &bBarrels&r, &bShulker Boxes&r, and &bBackapcks&r to this bad boy as you want, and they'll link in automagically to your storage system (as long as you link them together of course)."
		""
		"The &bStorage Tool&r, which you're gonna need to do the aformentioned linking, allows you to lock storage containers, turn displays on and off, and surprise surprise, link/unlink storage containers from your controller."
	]
	quest.312BDD942CB50EAA.quest_desc: [
		"Still with me? Awesome!"
		""
		"Right-click the &bAndesite&r with a &bMenril Chunk&r to make a &bLapis Block&r, then break the &bLapis Block&r and reap the sweet, sweet rewards."
	]
	quest.319040C0145ADE7C.quest_desc: [
		"Already got the &bCobblestone&r? That was quick. "
		""
		"I'd suggest making yourself some new tools about now, this time out of stone. These will get you into the next stages where we're really going to ramp things up! "
	]
	quest.33D6DFE0C629D53F.quest_desc: ["You know how in the olden days, you used to have to jump on this thing to make it work? Well, we can enlist something else to do the jumping for us! Pop one of these guys on top of the &bSqueezer&r, then use a &bButton&r or &bLever&r to get it up in the air. While it's in the air, shift right click the other &bArmor Stand&r onto the &bSqueezer&r and  then with some clever &bRedstone&r (a clock or an observer will do nicely) you can auto reset the &bSqueezer&r and fling the &bArmor Stands&r into the air on a loop!"]
	quest.34DC4EABAE6102A6.quest_desc: [
		"Okay, so the &bVoid Chassis&r is the actual cornerstone of Ender IO machines. I mis-spoke. "
		""
		"Make some of these in order to make some cool machinery!"
	]
	quest.353080FB3F7DF27F.quest_desc: ["This drawer is just like the last one. It can hold 2048 items, but you can store two different things in here! Crazy! "]
	quest.35AFC02F66924F27.quest_desc: ["Upgrades are available for all of the &bFunctional Drawers&r. There are many tiers, each one basically doubling the capacity of the tier before it. Start here with a &bCopper Upgrade&r to give you twice the base storage and if you want to keep going higher, feel free!"]
	quest.363CC56EDAF6419B.quest_desc: [
		"This machine we're naking here needs A LOT of power. Like A LOT a lot. So we're going to need two power sources for redundancy."
		""
		"One of them is from Powah and the other (this one) is from Applied Energistics. Get them both running and we'll never run out of power!"
	]
	quest.363FAF8F0220A5CC.quest_desc: ["Making a &bFurnace&r will help you get better materials later on, but for the time being it'll also help you with cooking food. There will be other, faster options as we progress, but this basic one will be enough to get us started."]
	quest.393D7A5EB9814B7B.quest_desc: [
		"Earlier, you would have made some &bVariable Cards&r. Take one of them over to the &bLogic Programmer&r and on the left side, choose \"Recipe\". "
		""
		"In the crafting box that appears, place three &bGravels&r along the top and in the right side, place a piece of &bFlint&r. Then, take your &bVariable Card&r and put it into the bottom right slot where the green check mark is."
		""
		"Congratulations, you've made your first auto crafting recipe! Take it and place it into the &bCrafting Interface&r that you made earlier, then check your storage system and you should be able to automatically make &bFlint&r! "
		""
		"Just repeat that process for whatever you want to make automatically in the future! "
	]
	quest.3A0954BAC3FCC9AE.quest_desc: [
		"&bEther Gas&r. This one will take a bit of planning. "
		""
		"There's a boss in the world called The Wither. If you can manage to trap one, and then stick a &bDrill&r above its head, you'll be able to harvest him to get some of this &bEther Gas&r. I'd suggest making a chamber out of a wither proof material, and you'll definitely need a &bStasis Chamber&r and a lot of power to keep him there. Collect the gas for making &bSupreme Machine Frames&r!"
	]
	quest.3A4D33EDC5BDB457.quest_desc: [
		"The &bMagmator&r uses &bLava&r for RF generation. If you have a way of getting a lot of &bLava&r, (some sort of tank perhaps) then this might be a good choice."
		""
		"The top tier of this machine will output 40,000 RF per tick. Pretty handy!"
	]
	quest.3AD84B704C9E0FA7.quest_desc: [
		"What is a &bDiamond&r but &bCoal&r that has been compressed over thousands of years?"
		""
		"Well, we don't have thousands of years, but what we do have is access to an unlimited amount of &bCoal&r. Make a &bCompressed Coal Block&r, and get yourself a bunch of &bDeepslate&r for the next ore!"
	]
	quest.3B4BE2A8B59E0181.quest_desc: [
		"Ah, &bFerricore&r. This stuff is ferrigood. "
		""
		"If you take some &bIron Blocks&r and place them on top of the &bPrimogel Goo&r block you just made, it will convert to &bFerricore Ore&r. You can then smelt that in any &bFurnace&r to make ingots!"
		""
		"If you have shaders turned on, it'll appear that nothing is happening until it does. Shaders off, you can see the whole process!"
	]
	quest.3BADDEDCA6125511.quest_desc: [
		"You can also point your &bCrafting Interface&r at a &bChest&r, have the items that you need to craft sent into the chest and then distributed to other machines for processing (like with Xnet for example). The system will recognize the completed craft if you have an &bImporter&r that pulls the resulting item back into the storage system."
		""
		"You can also use a &bVariable Store&r and some other wizardry to set some specific items to keep a certain number in your inventory. Play around with things, use the book &aOn The Dynamics Of Integration&r from your &bAkashic Tome&r to really go in depth with this mod!"
	]
	quest.3C0332E742535895.quest_desc: ["Wood, now in raspberry flavor!"]
	quest.3C936149A45663B0.quest_desc: [
		"&bCelestigems&r are used for making higher tier machines, armors and weapons but beware, they're not exactly cheap."
		""
		"Maybe you've seen some dungeons on your travels and found a bunch of &bDiamond&r gear on the lower levels? I suggest taking some of that and running it through your &bSalvager&r (remember that thing?) to reclaim some of the &bDiamonds&r from those items and make this process a little easier. Otherwise, I hope you've got &bCoal&r automated and are producing LOTS of it."
	]
	quest.3D09913257A3B16D.quest_desc: ["This is where the magic happens. Or at least where the magic ends up. The final piece of the puzzle, the machine's output slot!"]
	quest.3DAD9766E1582662.quest_desc: ["This little guy right here is quite possibly the most convenient upgrade to the portable storage market in the history of ever."]
	quest.3DB0765B4AA72713.quest_desc: [
		"It's a good idea to have somewhere to store all of that Powah you're making. That's what this fella does. "
		""
		"This basic one will store 4,000 RF and the top tier stores 2,000,000 RF. Use this as a buffer between your power gen and machines and if your generator runs out of Powah for any reason, the energy cell will keep it running for a while. "
	]
	quest.3DDD642331291AE3.quest_desc: [
		"If you see one of these lying around, grab it. Grab a few!"
		""
		"If you hit a &bDiamond Ore Block&r with one of these, it'll change into the most coveted of all the blocks... &bEmerald&r!"
	]
	quest.3E05B407B9296A54.quest_desc: [
		"Did you make one of these earlier? Great! Make another one! "
		""
		"This is the glue that holds the two halves of our final multiblock machine together! Please make one."
	]
	quest.3F7FD3F5FE967616.quest_desc: [
		"And now, whack that &bGold&r onto the &bBasalt&r to make your first &bAncient Debris&r!"
		""
		"Congratulations! You've mastered ore generation!"
	]
	quest.3FBA40690AE6D713.quest_desc: [
		"By now, you should have this process pretty much mastered. But just in case you don't, we'll go over it one more time."
		""
		"This time, you need some &bMenril Chunks&r - you can get them from those blue trees that are dotted around all over the place. Now, get yourself a bunch of &bAndesite&r and make a &bStone Generator&r for unlimited &bAndesite&r blocks."
	]
	quest.3FCCA87A14EF1A85.quest_desc: ["This &bSolar Panel&r will produce power passively from the sun! The downside being, of course, it doesn't produce power at night time. Once again, the top tier can only produce 2,000 RF per tick, but these can be joined  together to make large Powah arrays."]
	quest.40AB1EB0FC3F32E4.quest_desc: [
		"Seen any &bEmeralds&r lying around? Energize those, too! But you'll need a lot of power to do so! "
		""
		"This will get you even more Powah, faster than ever before!"
	]
	quest.45452869BA09634F.quest_desc: ["&bModular Routers&r can be used to automate a bunch of stuff. In this case, we're going to need two of them to build our wonderful machine."]
	quest.463D2805F0CBA322.quest_desc: [
		"So this little thing can be used to upgrade other little things into better little things, or bigger little things. You'll need this to upgrade some of the items from your Powah setup. Get to crafting!"
		""
		"Side note, you can also speed things along by energizing items in their block forms!"
	]
	quest.467E30E27BCD16F1.quest_desc: ["If you've made a deep hole into the ground and seen that stripy block called \"bedrock\" you can throw some &bRedstone&r on it, place an &bObsidian Block&r above and left click it and make yourself some &bFlux dust&r!"]
	quest.47EB85DD0031881C.quest_desc: [
		"Need to transport energy? Make some of these! "
		""
		"This is the base level, higher tiers are available to transport more power more quickly."
		""
		"AND you can put several of these in the same block space!"
	]
	quest.4854E1161D03BC88.quest_desc: [
		"Want to automatically craft things? You can! Sort of. No, you totally can. Sort of."
		""
		"Anyway, you'll need one of these attached to a &bLogic Cable&r, pointing at a &bCrafting Table&r (or a storage) in order to automatically craft things using your Integrated Dynamics Storage System (TM) "
	]
	quest.48F9B8BD9358A743.quest_desc: ["I know it looks delicious, but trust me when I tell you not to eat it."]
	quest.4B96DC802C8FDF82.quest_desc: [
		"Okay, let's get started. This is going to be a bit of a process, so I'll take it slowly."
		""
		"Firstly, you're going to need some &bLogs&r. Any &bLogs&r will do. Just break one with your hand, we'll work on getting tools later."
	]
	quest.4BB4152EEB3DE69E.quest_desc: [
		"Just as you can make a bunch of cool stuff with &bFerricore&r, you can make a bunch of cooler stuff with &bBlazegold&r! Same process to make it as &bFerricore&r, just use &bGold Blocks&r instead and then check out the uses! You'll need these to make &bAdvanced Machine Frames&r and you'll need those to make the next tier of Goo. "
		""
		"Goo-d luck!"
	]
	quest.4C8C312A667C43C8.quest_desc: [
		"We're flying now! One step closer to bringing us all home!"
		""
		"Keep those &bSupreme Machine Frames&r going, you're going to need them!"
	]
	quest.4EFAC50CC365FB5C.quest_desc: [
		"&bConduit Binder Composite&r is the cornerstone of Ender IO conduits. You'll need some of this, no matter which type of conduit you intend to make."
		""
		"And Ender IO has all sorts of conduits that you can use, so make some of this stuff and then run it through a &bFurnace&r (or your &bAlloy Smelter&r) to make it in to &bConduit Binder&r."
	]
	quest.4F4E68A3EBA3CA21.quest_desc: [
		"This is it! The final machine! What we've been building towards all this time! "
		""
		"Make the &bController&r (click on the controller above to see the recipe) and I'll swap it out for the &bVillager Summoner&r!"
		""
		"That's right, smack this bad boy down, hit it with the &bBlueprint&r and then assemble it. Once everything is in place, the villagers will start returning! "
		""
		"Every 30 seconds one of us will be transported back home again!"
	]
	quest.4FA0172B9B390474.quest_desc: [
		"Storage? In Chests? What kind of pleb do you take me for?!"
		""
		"Make an &bInscriber&r, though. You'll need this to make your AE2 system really shine!"
	]
	quest.502A773FAC56BB2D.quest_desc: [
		"Ah, the humble &bChest&r. The back bone of all storage for miners and crafters!"
		""
		"You'll find you have several options for organizing your storage going forward, but it all starts here!"
	]
	quest.5204B29825161326.quest_desc: [
		"I've heard stories about a place called \"The Nether\". Sounds made up to me."
		""
		"Pop over there anyway, grab yourself some &bGlowstone&r and a bunch of &bBlackstone&r, and I'll meet you back here."
		""
		"Ready? Break!"
	]
	quest.538A09875DB3E71D.quest_desc: ["Flux Network or Powah?"]
	quest.538A09875DB3E71D.title: "Power Yourself"
	quest.539CDBE232559A4F.quest_desc: ["Okay, to make this machine you're going to need some of this stuff. Be careful, though, in order to make this you're going to encounter a pretty angry dude. "]
	quest.53F18385D78EB035.quest_desc: [
		"At some point, you're going to need to make yourself some Powah. We'll do it with ingenuity—and by killing a bunch of Spiders!"
		""
		"Get a &bSpider Eye&r, ferment it, and add a whole lot of &bCalcite&r. It's out in the world, I promise."
	]
	quest.55783B00E36A4AAE.quest_desc: [
		"You should have noticed by now that there's no &bCoal&r anywhere - It's all been taken by the robots. Your only fuel source at the moment is wood, like those &bLogs&r you grabbed earlier. "
		""
		"Luckily, those &bLogs&r are more than just a cheap and easily renewable fuel source: you can also burn them to make &bCharcoal&r, and &bCharcoal&r is a much better fuel source than those &bLogs&r alone!"
	]
	quest.55C2222EF7EF00B8.quest_desc: [
		"Stay with me on this, because it's going to sound crazy. Mobs in boxes. Is your mind blown yet?"
		""
		"Make one of these boxes, stick the card that you got earlier into it and it'll start producing items that you can use to help you on your way!"
		""
		"I suggest finding a &bCow&r card as quickly as you can, but there are several cards that will help you on your journey. Collect them all! (tm)"
	]
	quest.576BBC8B603DD337.quest_desc: [
		"Mob farms were covered elsewhere in this textbook. Please refer back to them if you need more information. "
		""
		"We're going to need a couple of these for our final machine. Hopefully you've figured out how to make &bNetherite&r by now!"
	]
	quest.57E8A98DD1DD57FD.quest_desc: [
		"You can generate &bPink Slime&r with a &bMob Slaughter Factory&r. You can use it as a substitute for the normal green slime, but why would you do that? That's crazy talk! "
		""
		"Get yourself a bucket of this, tip it out on the ground to get a &bPink Slime&r. Then get it before it runs away! Or keep the bucket handy and use it in a &bDissolution Chamber&r to make an &bAdvanced Machine Frame&r."
	]
	quest.58B07F8EFFFFD0BF.quest_desc: ["In order for you to make some of the stuff from this mod, you're going to need a &bSqueezer&r. You know, for squeezing. Make one of these and a &bDrying Basin&r and let me know when you're ready for the next step!"]
	quest.5A5EF50C159DDB3E.quest_desc: ["This machine uses different heat sources to make Powah. Pump some water inside of this and have some &bLava&r underneath, and it will produce passive Powah. It is, however, not as good at the higher tiers as the other machines here are, producing only 2,000 RF per tick at the top level."]
	quest.5B2FD1962F1354E8.quest_desc: [
		"I'll give you the basics for generation with Powah. All of these machines are upgradable to higher tiers with better outputs. I'm sure you can figure out how to do that with JEI. "
		""
		"This guy here makes Powah by burning &bCoal&r. You may even have an automatic &bCoal&r set up running by now, so this machine should be pretty trivial. The base machine makes a small amount of Powah, but the top tier makes 40,000 RF per tick! "
	]
	quest.5D62DE4375A3FEBB.quest_desc: ["If you upgrade your &bBank&r, you can store more stuff! And more stacks of more stuff! Exciting!"]
	quest.5D78A9540D4FDB2C.quest_desc: [
		"Let's keep the upgrades rollin' in. &bIron&r this time, for more items and more stacks!"
		""
		"There's a bunch more upgrades you can add to the &bBank&r. Don't let me stop you from making it HUGE."
	]
	quest.5E08463F2739AEDD.quest_desc: ["You can't automatically craft anything without giving your system some recipes. Those recipes are stored on &bPatterns&r. You'll want a few &bPatterns&r for all the automation you're bound to be doing, so let's make a cool dozen. Less two. It's called a Newstone dozen! (Pattern Pending - Speak to Bevarin if you like/dislike this joke)"]
	quest.5E921DEE8BFD75A5.quest_desc: [
		"Need to transport fluids? Make some of these! "
		""
		"Please note, you probably don't want to transport &bLava&r with this pipe. There's a higher tier for that."
	]
	quest.60334DDB85D5662D.quest_desc: [
		"I pity the machine frame! "
		""
		"Sorry. I don't know what came over me. "
		""
		"Anyway, in order for you to get into Industrial Foregoing (and a couple of other mods) you're going to need to smash out some &bMachine Frames&r. Let's start with a &bPity Machine Frame&r. You'll need this to get into generating &bLatex&r for &bRubber&r and &bPlastic&r production, and you're going to need &bPlastic&r if you want to automate some of your processes - like a mob farm, for example."
	]
	quest.60845C1479A6E29D.quest_desc: ["The base &bReactor&r will output 1,000 RF per tick, while the top tier one will do 500,000 RF per tick. This is obviously the best option, but it's also the most expensive, both to build and to keep running. "]
	quest.627D8762F9AD4E98.quest_desc: [
		"A &bMenril Log&r in your &bSqueezer&r (auto or otherwise) will produce a block of &bCrystalized Menril&r if you aim the little channel running through the middle of the &bSqueezer&r and your &bDrying Basin&r."
		""
		"Let it dry and grab yourself some &bCrystalized Menril&r!"
	]
	quest.63778C604341452A.quest_desc: ["You may notice when you're out there fighting the robots, some of them may drop one of these cards. If they do, don't discard it. Keep it handy, because it may come in useful in the future!"]
	quest.640D84A511D8C4AA.quest_desc: [
		"If you're not happy with an Integrated Dynamics storage system, you can go more powerful with an AE2 system. Seen any meteors while you've been wandering around? Get yourself into the middle of one of those to really get your AE2 system moving."
		""
		"Eventually, you'll want to start automatically crafting things using AE2. You'll need these for that. Please do so."
	]
	quest.64ACF192810361FC.quest_desc: ["Now slap that &bDeepslate&r block with your &bCompressed &bCoal&r Block&r, and we bypass all those thousands of years to make &bDiamonds&r!"]
	quest.66792995242B2112.quest_desc: ["Those &bBlock Generators&r you made earlier are also a required component of our final machine. Make two of them and add them to this list."]
	quest.67EAD9CE78F79319.quest_desc: [
		"Take that &bIron-laden Beef&r you found earlier and right-click it on some &bTuff&r. You should get some nice, lovely, &bIron Ore&r."
		""
		"Break it and get the &bRaw &bIron&r, and we're good to go!"
	]
	quest.6805031225D109E4.quest_desc: [
		"These are here for the final machine mostly just as decoration. But don't they look neat! "
		""
		"You need 6 of them and they will structurally hold the whole machine togther. So not really decoration after all. "
	]
	quest.686AD58469D60BE2.quest_desc: ["&bGlowstone&r and &bBlackstone&r will make &bGold Ore&r! You know the drill by now!"]
	quest.69C10526FDC82FF1.quest_desc: [
		"Got enough &bLogs&r? Excellent! Let's get to breaking those down to planks and making a &bCrafting Table&r. This thing will be your best friend for the next while, so get used to it!"
		""
		"Once you have that made, you're going to need some basic tools. Let's start with a &bPickaxe&r to get you going. One made of wood will be perfect to get the ball rolling. Use that and go and grab yourself some &bCobblestone&r!"
	]
	quest.6A33F299EA6E9F57.quest_desc: [
		"If you’ve found this book, it means our time here is over. The world has been overrun by machines, and our colony had no choice but to leave. The settlement you stand in was once our proud home - &6Newstone Hollow&r."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The land here was once fertile, and the caves were full of precious ores. But then they came: an army of machines that stripped almost every last resource. They devoured our crops, dismantled our equipment, and carved away the very metals beneath our feet. They left us with nothing but dust and ruins."
		""
		"But... I had a plan. A blueprint for rebuilding all that we lost. A vision of a new &6Newstone Hollow&r, bigger and better than before. We had to depart before we could make that dream come true, but I’ve left this book behind for anyone who might discover these remains of civilization."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Should you find this record, use it as your guide. Forge new machines, reclaim the soil, and make this broken world thrive again. Let the seeds of a second &6Newstone Hollow&r take root with your hands."
	]
	quest.6A33F299EA6E9F57.quest_subtitle: "The Ghost of our Greatness"
	quest.6ACDFA92314B29BF.quest_desc: [
		"This one's a bit of a stretch so stick with me: &bGranite&r and &bHoney Bottles&r. "
		""
		"We're going to need some of both of these, so repeat the same process you did to make stone but replace the &bTriple Compressed Stone&r with a &bTriple Compressed &bGranite&r. Everything else is the same! "
	]
	quest.6B0C0F3BF7F62D14.quest_desc: ["&bNetherrack&r and &bBone Block&r makes &bQuartz&r! This one feels important. I'd try to keep this one going if you can."]
	quest.6C19D96CD0EC20B2.quest_desc: ["&bFlux Cores&r are made using &bFlux Dust&r and some other bits and pieces. You'll need them to make the Flux Networks work. If you send some of your Powah into this baby, you'll be able to bypass those cables you made earlier and have true wireless power for your machines."]
	quest.6EE96F930ABAB866.quest_desc: ["If you want to get to the higher tiers of the Powah machines, you're going to need to start making this stuff. Go back this \"Nether\" place and get yourself some &bBlaze Rods&r. You'll need them for this quest!"]
	quest.6EEC8470B772ADE0.quest_desc: [
		"Sophisticated Storage. The more classy version of vanilla storage. You can do so many things with this mod, if you can master it you'll wonder why you use anything else! "
		""
		"Start off by making a &bSophisticated Chest&r. Any old &bChest&r will do. You can do it by combining a &bChest&r with a &bRedstone Torch&r, or sticking one in the middle of a normal &bChest&r recipe to skip a step. "
	]
	quest.6EEC8470B772ADE0.title: "Basic Sophistication"
	quest.6FC9C4EA03935AEF.quest_desc: [
		"&bPaper&r or &bPlastic&r? Hopefully &bPlastic&r because that's where we're headed now. "
		""
		"Make yourself a &bFluid Extractor&r using that &bPity Machine Frame&r you just made and slap that baby next to a log. It'll pull out &bLatex&r and eventually, you'll get a bucket of it. Grab that!"
	]
	quest.703DBA1F787C4AE7.quest_desc: [
		"Remember how I told you you'd need a lot of &bStone&r earlier? Here's why: the &bStone Block Generator&r will make new stone from literally nothing! Well, nothing and some &bLava&r and &bWater&r. And a &bTriple Compressed Block of Stone&r. Why triple compressed? It wouldn't work with anything less!"
		""
		"Put the compressed block under the generator, a bucket of water on one side and a bucket of lava on the other. Bingo, free stone! "
		""
		"Then, you'll need some &bFlint&r. You can get that by just mining up some &bGravel&r (if you're lucky) or crafting three &bGravel&r together in your &bCrafting Table&r. Remember that thing!?"
	]
	quest.70A1FBB484C19C8A.quest_desc: [
		"Your first real step in upgrading things is to throw some &bGold&r and &bIron&r into your &bEnergizing Orb&r and transform them into &bEngergized Steel&r. "
		""
		"You can then use that &bEnergized Steel&r to make other things in the Powah ouvre. Is that how you spell ouvre? It'll do."
	]
	quest.72D31DDB8ED2D8EB.quest_desc: [
		"Want a place to offload all that good stuff you've been collecting? Make yourself a &bBank Dock&r, doc!"
		""
		"This baby can auto-import stuff directly from your &bBank&r and put it into a storage system for you!"
	]
	quest.74DA7CC368174109.quest_desc: ["The &bFunctional Storage Controller&r works much the same as the &bSophisticated Controller&r. Smack some sort of storage connector to this thing and connect up some &bDrawers&r with the linking tool and you can then access everything that's inside them. Niiiiice."]
	quest.75EC43EFD883A9E3.quest_desc: ["It's crafting anywhere you want to be!"]
	quest.7CAE333CB8721853.quest_desc: ["This thing is where you can set the recipes that you need for the auto crafter to automatically craft. It makes sense, logically!"]
	quest.7D708C05F94D4748.quest_desc: ["Functional Storage puts the \"fun\" in Functional Storage. Remember back in the olden days when you could make drawers to store things in? Well you still can! That's right, this little fella can hold up to 2048 items inside it in its default configuration. Make yourself one. Heck, make a few. You're going to need them!"]
	quest.7E6CA7E720B81BA6.quest_desc: [
		"In order for you to make more Powah, you're going to need a few of these bad boys. Why does no-one ever talk about the good boys? "
		""
		"Never mind, let's jut concentrate on what we're doing here now and make some dielectric casings so we can move on with our lives."
	]
	quest.7EAEB150A6816327.quest_desc: ["Need to store a bunch of fluid and have easy access to it? Make one of these. There are even upgrades for this that will allow you to generate inifinite amounts of certain fluids. Very handy!"]
	quest.7ECE99AD03E6A6B6.quest_desc: [
		"This little fella here connects to your storage system. You can do it the hard way by sticking one of these on every &bChest&r or &bBarrel&r you have, or if you have a &bSophisticated Storage Controller&r or a &bFunctional Storage Controller&r, you can connect one of these to that and it'll link to everything that's connected to the controller instead!"
		""
		"Easy!"
	]
	task.273B2F9BDD1049AF.title: "Any #minecraft:&bLogs&r"
	task.28F8EA0265591C00.title: "Power Yoursellf"
	task.3FCD8876E933AFFD.title: "Beginning at the End"
	task.4F1CF595ED8EA109.title: "Any #easy_mob_farm:mob_farm_templates"
	task.65649676F85245FE.title: "Supremely Useful"
	task.67C10D22C0CF0AFD.title: "Any #sophisticatedstorage:base_tier_wooden_storage"
	task.7C50FEE74497772E.title: "Any #Powah:player_transmitters"
}
